docs/program/DECISIONS.md:20:| OSD-D13 | Outline licence | Outlines derived from a publisher's data carry that publisher's licence, not CC0: each feature gets `licence` from its record, and `records/LICENSE` dedicates only the hand-written records and catalogue metadata | DEFAULT 23 Oct (E03 review) |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:22:| OSD-D15 | Licence statement for outlines from a register | A publisher's own entry in its national open-data catalogue (Geonorge for Sodir: FactMaps data and service, NLOD) counts as the publisher's licence statement for outlines derived from that register when the service itself carries none. A version discrepancy between catalogue and terms page is recorded in the record's `known_issues`, not resolved by us | DEFAULT 23 Oct (E03 inbox) |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:26:| OSD-D22 | Deposited origins: may a maintainer deposit files a publisher hands only to registered persons, when the licence allows redistribution? | Yes, as a verification fact with who/when/licence text captured, never for `restricted` or `unknown`, under the OSD-D6 caps (E41). The person registers; the tool never does | DEFAULT 28 Oct (planner), owner may overturn |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:29:| OSD-D26 | The site becomes one page, "the map as a shop" (search bar, a list that follows the map window, the map; Filters is one button; a round green plus per row, a tick when in the bag; a small icon for how the dataset is obtained; Ophiolite look: Merriweather, Roboto, night blue; base map in familiar colours; Flat and Globe; no legend on the map; no colour on the map for what is in the bag). Supersedes OSD-D3 for the new page | Family `charters/MAP-AS-A-SHOP-family.md`, E47, E48, E53 | DECIDED by the owner 25 Nov 2026 (Paper boards Shop 01–06) |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:30:| OSD-D27 | Outlines: one exclusive switch Countries / Provinces / Basins, later Licences; an area is drawn only when a dataset sits in it; every drawn area is clickable and filters the list; Names on / off, one name per area. "Sits in it" is counted when the catalogue is built, from real well positions and survey outlines; a dataset without positions uses the middle of its box; a country-wide dataset counts for the country | E46 (the count), E48 (the switch) | DECIDED by the owner 25 Nov 2026 (board Open 01) |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:31:| OSD-D28 | Sources for the outlines: countries and provinces Natural Earth (public domain); basins USGS "Geologic Provinces of the World" (use constraints none, credit U.S. Geological Survey) | `areas/SOURCES.md` with E46 slice 1 | DECIDED by the owner 25 Nov 2026 |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:32:| OSD-D29 | Licences: no free world layer exists; read per country from the regulator on a schedule. Order United Kingdom, Norway, United States; then Canada and Australia once their terms are read. Draw licences, only those holding a dataset; name the block in the dataset row. The schedule is a stated exception to rule R6 (no timers): a weekly workflow that opens a pull request, never pushes to main | E51 | DECIDED by the owner 25 Nov 2026 (board Open 02); the weekly period and the pull-request form are the supervisor's DEFAULT |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:33:| OSD-D30 | The bag has three ways out: download the files, get a Python file, open in Ophiolite. The "Open in Ophiolite" button is not shipped (absent, not disabled) until the whole path works; Ophiolite's supervisor sends the landing address shape | E47 (bag), E49 (Python file); the button waits outside this family | DECIDED by the owner 25 Nov 2026 (boards Shop 04, 05) |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:34:| OSD-D31 | Speed: map usable within 2 s, 60 pictures a second while moving, no download for an area visited before in the same visit, no download of our files on a return visit; the practices of board Shop 06; order of work: keep the present host, measure a return visit in a real browser first, add a browser cache only if that shows downloads. Four measurements are owed (real laptop and phone, return visit in a browser, zooming, globe with all wells) | E50, numbers in its PR | DECIDED by the owner 25 Nov 2026 (board Shop 06) |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:37:| OSD-D34 | Work in progress for this family | R1 (two coding lanes plus one records lane) is a floor, not a cap, for E46–E53: as many Opus lanes side by side as have disjoint claimed paths; the claims board keeps them apart; the controller's disk is checked before a lane is added | DECIDED by the owner 25 Nov 2026 ("open as many agents as you need … so that we don't wait for features too long") |
docs/program/DECISIONS.md:38:| OSD-D35 | How a record says it covers a country | record/6, optional `region.national: true`: the publisher presents the dataset as covering the country in `region.country`. A publisher fact, filled by E52 from the publisher's page; replaces the prototype's guess from the size of the box | DEFAULT (supervisor, 25 Nov 2026) |
