docs/program/charters/E40-starter-project-contract-CODEX-REVIEW.log:3365:- **Manifest/4 is not the proposed pack representation.** Its entries contain `assets`, collection identity and publisher licence fields; attribution is an enum, not arbitrary lines (`schema/manifest.schema.json:66`, `:90`). `src/osd/get.py:146` generates attribution from those fields. Specify an exact, lossless mapping; if impossible, version the manifest contract and claim the reader/schema changes with backwards-compatibility tests.
docs/program/charters/E40-starter-project-contract-CODEX-REVIEW.log:3368:- **Licence computation is undefined for disagreement or null SPDX.** Design 2c constrains SPDX only “when they agree”; it also drops publisher terms and prescribed statements (`schema/record.schema.json:44`). Preserve source licence objects; refuse unsupported combinations until an explicit policy exists, rather than infer compatibility from `share_alike`.
docs/program/charters/E40-starter-project-contract-CODEX-REVIEW.log:3386:- **E43:** Its page needs kinds/counts, decisions and oracle data; E40 design 3 guarantees only targets, licence and URLs. Define the complete published projection in E40 so E43 does not invent a second data contract.
