docs/program/charters/E49-the-python-file-CODEX-REVIEW.log:13:You are a fresh, independent senior reviewer of one epic charter in the Open Subsurface Data project (a verified catalogue of open subsurface datasets: YAML records -> verifier levels -> outlines -> STAC/GeoJSON catalogue -> static MapLibre map; Python package src/osd, tests in tests/, schemas in schema/, site in site/). Read docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/ENGINEERING.md, AGENTS.md, docs/program/charters/MAP-AS-A-SHOP-family.md, then the charter docs/program/charters/E49-the-python-file.md. This is the single review round for a kernel charter (OSD-D8). Read-only: modify nothing. VERIFY every claim in "Context today" against the code at HEAD and cite file:line. Then judge: (1) Verdict APPROVE or REWORK in one sentence. (2) Factual errors and Context verification. (3) Contract problems: schema or API shapes that are ambiguous, cannot be implemented as written, or will force a breaking change later (the family's later epics E48, E51, E52 build on this). (4) Acceptance lines that can pass without the outcome being delivered, or that cannot be tested offline. (5) Guards missing a mutation. (6) Scope: what should move out or in; conflicts with the paths other open lanes hold (docs/program/CLAIMS.md). (7) Risks to the gate (make check offline under 120 s) and to the rule that network is allowed only in named commands. Number every finding (F1, F2, ...) so each can be dispositioned. Be concrete and brief; do not restate the charter. The owner's decisions (OSD-D26 to OSD-D31, OSD-D34 in docs/program/DECISIONS.md) are fixed and not up for review.
