docs/program/charters/E19-vocabulary-from-the-records-lanes-CODEX-REVIEW.md:1:**1. Verdict: REWORK.** The charter relies on a nonexistent NRCan record, contradicts schema-versioning rules, and would break manifest compatibility while dropping new licence restrictions.
docs/program/charters/E19-vocabulary-from-the-records-lanes-CODEX-REVIEW.md:7:- Confirmed: four access values, 18 kinds ending in `source-list`, and the seven-field closed licence object (`schema/record.schema.json:29`, `:36`, `:50`). Counted **92** dataset YAML records.
docs/program/charters/E19-vocabulary-from-the-records-lanes-CODEX-REVIEW.md:18:- **Manifest breakage:** `purchase` is rejected by `schema/manifest.schema.json:86`; new terms disappear through Python and browser licence allowlists (`src/osd/manifest.py:42`; `site/app.js:289`). Extend/version the manifest contract and both writers/readers; prove exact licence preservation through both paths.
docs/program/charters/E19-vocabulary-from-the-records-lanes-CODEX-REVIEW.md:37:- Manifest compatibility and complete rights preservation cross **E06/E09** (`E06-retrieval-by-manifest.md:68`; `E09-ophiolite-reads-the-catalogue.md:37`). These are necessary integration work, not optional follow-ups.
