docs/program/charters/E41-deposited-origins-CODEX-REVIEW.md:1:**1. Verdict: REWORK** — Deposit persistence, licence evidence, and catalogue retrieval are underspecified, so the acceptance criteria can pass without delivering a durable, downloadable deposit.
docs/program/charters/E41-deposited-origins-CODEX-REVIEW.md:9:- **Confirmed F3 facts:** registration, absent manifest URL, licence and replacement-release note match `records/terranubis/f3-demo-2020.yaml:7–22`. Its current L1 ceiling follows from missing `manifest_url` (`src/osd/verify.py:458–460`), not a general prohibition on registration datasets.
docs/program/charters/E41-deposited-origins-CODEX-REVIEW.md:17:- **Licence capture is incomplete.** Design 1 records hashes; acceptance 1 supplies only one captured page. Existing verification fetches `licence.url`, normalizes and retains its text (`src/osd/verify.py:639–662`, `:728–730`). Require separately identified publisher and licence captures, source URLs, capture dates, retained text and recomputed hashes; a publisher-page hash cannot substitute for licence capture.
docs/program/charters/E41-deposited-origins-CODEX-REVIEW.md:27:- **A2:** tests only licence-hash presence; empty inventory, fabricated hashes, failed L1 checks and stale evidence remain untested. Test those negatives and the separate `reason()` output.
docs/program/charters/E41-deposited-origins-CODEX-REVIEW.md:28:- **A3:** “over 20 GB” misses an erroneous `>` boundary check; `unknown` misses a guard allowing `restricted`. Test exactly `CAP_BYTES`, both forbidden rights values and empty inventory.
docs/program/charters/E41-deposited-origins-CODEX-REVIEW.md:36:- E40 design 1 already reserves `deposited`; E41 should supply and validate its custody evidence, not redefine starter inputs or pack licence computation.
