docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.md-28-- “Overlay replaced by copy” is not a precise mutation: copying files into an existing directory already overlays them. Assert both replacement of an existing result and preservation of a missing shard’s result; mutate destination deletion and overwrite suppression separately.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.md-29-- Retaining every old file and verifying nothing can satisfy runtime, level-count and schema checks. Require fresh-result IDs to equal the complete checkout record set for the successful timing run; retained results must not count as verified.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.md:30:- No acceptance test proves concurrent dispatch preservation, fresh-only recovery reporting, or the doubled-catalogue 40-minute promise. Add offline orchestration tests and a defined scaling measurement.
