docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log-6286-- Confirmed: one hosted job, 60-minute timeout, earlier-result restoration, `--outline-inputs`, status and dead-link reporting: `.github/workflows/verify.yml:13–60`.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log:6287:- Confirmed: full validation, force-push and Pages dispatch: `.github/workflows/verify.yml:82–95`. Qualification missing from Context: these three operations run **only for dispatches on main**.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log:6288:- Confirmed: verification is serial (`src/osd/verify.py:791–807`); the CLI invokes it directly (`src/osd/cli.py:66`). No concurrency group exists in the complete workflow; overlapping main dispatches can overwrite results.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log-6289-- The quoted durations, concurrency of historical runs and nine ArcGIS inputs are historical observations, **not verified by HEAD**. Attach run metadata, checked-out SHA and actual processed-record counts.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log-6290-- “176 records counted after E31 merged during the run” does not establish that the run verified 176 records: checkout precedes verification, with no subsequent main refresh (`.github/workflows/verify.yml:18–40`). A later merge cannot enlarge that checkout.
--
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log-6294-- **Earlier results are needed inside each shard.** Design 2 mentions downloading them only in the finishing job. Verification reads previous results for licence changes, blocked history and L4 carry-forward (`src/osd/verify.py:567–569,610,734–743,800`). Restore one common results snapshot into every shard; upload only freshly generated files belonging to that shard, never its entire restored directory.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log-6295-- **“Does what the single job does today” breaks recovery reporting after shard failure.** Today the workflow passes `--verified all` for an empty selection (`.github/workflows/verify.yml:60`); retained L1 results could then close issues without a fresh observation (`src/osd/report.py:91–109`). Pass exactly the freshly verified IDs; when none succeeded, skip issue mutation explicitly.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log:6296:- **The hash/budget contract changes silently.** Every process gets a 2 GiB budget (`src/osd/verify.py:78,293,789`), so N shards permit N times the previous dispatch budget. Specify and justify a per-dispatch versus per-shard policy; preserve a dispatch cap through explicit shard allocations if that remains the contract.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log-6297-- **Empty selection is dangerous.** `verify_all(ids=[])` verifies everything (`src/osd/verify.py:792`). Require an empty shard to exit successfully without invoking verification; define index bounds, hash algorithm and encoding, and reject malformed shard arguments.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log-6298-- **Partial failure needs an executable policy.** Require independent shards to continue, define whether partial artifacts are discarded or accepted, validate artifact membership, and make the finishing job report incomplete coverage. Retain existing per-record JSON and use standard Actions artifacts.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log:6299:- **Concurrency must cover the whole read–verify–store transaction**, including explicit-ID main dispatches. `cancel-in-progress: false` alone does not retain every pending run; default concurrency replaces an existing pending run. Explicitly accept coalescing or use the documented `queue: max`, with a stated overflow policy. [GitHub workflow syntax](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-syntax#concurrency)
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log-6300-- **Host grouping conflicts with the fixed ID-hash design.** Choose one rule before implementation. Origin-host grouping also misses shared listing, licence and input hosts; measure those request hosts before accepting parallel pressure.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log:6301:- **Ownership is too narrow:** “`cli.py` verify arguments only” excludes the `cmd_verify` selection and empty-shard handling required at `src/osd/cli.py:63–66`. Claim that command’s dispatch logic explicitly.
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log-6302-
docs/program/charters/H2-verify-in-shards-CODEX-REVIEW.log-6303-**4. Acceptance loopholes**
